When the model is not Qwen3.5 on CUDA, the `max_active` function returns `1`.

This is explicitly handled in the function:

```rust
let Engine::Qwen35Cuda(_) = &loaded.model else {
    return 1;
};
```

If the model is not of type `Engine::Qwen35Cuda`, the function immediately returns `1` without performing any further GPU memory calculations. This behavior is also confirmed by the function's documentation:

> "Anything but Qwen3.5 on CUDA runs one request."

So, for any model that is not Qwen3.5 on CUDA, only a single request can run at a time.
